# The nightly log hygiene check (#174). Reads the day's journal, validates it
# against docs/4.4.7's schema, writes exceptions to its own log, and refreshes a
# marker object only on a clean run. It runs on rehearsal and production; it
# does not take the deploy lock, since it only reads the journal.
#
# Reads and writes nothing else (bar TLE_UPLOAD from the .env) — no accounts, no email, no driving of flows.
# The rare events are covered in CI, by the regression suite.
#
# **Four files travel together** into /opt/tile-lite-elite/, because the
# validator is useless without the schema and the schema is a repository
# document: check-log-hygiene-nightly.sh, check-log-hygiene.py, upload.sh (shared
# with the backup), and
# docs/4.4.7-log-events.md. There is no checkout on this host, so they are the
# image's payload: Turpin installs them as host files (`[[turpin.host_files]]`
# in app-profile.toml) at each deploy, and a change to one ships in the image.
# Until 0.10.3, the fallback deploy.sh still copies them. A deploy that does
# not install them leaves the host validating against last month's schema.
[Unit]
Description=Tile Lite Elite — validate the day's log against docs/4.4.7

[Service]
Type=oneshot
User=ubuntu
# The user must be able to read the journal: `usermod -aG systemd-journal ubuntu`.
ExecStart=/opt/tile-lite-elite/check-log-hygiene-nightly.sh
